# TaskDesk bootstrap configuration.
#
#   cp deploy/.env.example .env
#   $EDITOR .env
#   scripts/deploy.sh local
#
# scripts/deploy.sh generates any missing secret and never regenerates one that
# already has a value, so the two `openssl rand` lines below can be left as they
# are for a local install.
#
# Five required variables, six optional per-process switches, and that is the
# whole list the application reads. Everything else — storage, mail, identity
# providers, branding, features, roles — is configured in God Mode and stored in
# the database. The authority is docs/05-operations/configuration-reference.md;
# `pnpm check:env` fails the build on any other process.env read.

# --- Required ---------------------------------------------------------------

# Where configuration lives. In the shipped Compose stack this is composed from
# the POSTGRES_* variables below and set on the container, so leave it unset
# unless you are pointing at a database outside this stack.
# TASKDESK_DATABASE_URL=postgres://taskdesk:taskdesk@postgres:5432/taskdesk

# Decrypts plugin secrets. 64 hex characters: openssl rand -hex 32
# LOSE THIS AND EVERY CONFIGURED INTEGRATION MUST BE RECONFIGURED.
TASKDESK_ENCRYPTION_KEY=

# Session signing. 64 hex characters: openssl rand -hex 32
# Rotating it signs everyone out. There is no default and there must not be.
TASKDESK_AUTH_SECRET=

# Public origins. Two hostnames, separate cookie scopes.
TASKDESK_AGENT_URL=https://ticket.localhost
TASKDESK_PORTAL_URL=https://portal.localhost

# --- Optional ---------------------------------------------------------------

# Bind port. Never published in production.
TASKDESK_PORT=5173

# Required for multiple replicas. The shipped Compose stack sets it to the
# bundled Valkey; set it here only to point somewhere else.
# TASKDESK_VALKEY_URL=redis://valkey:6379

# all | web | jobs. Gates the in-process scheduler.
TASKDESK_ROLE=all

# Set ONLY during an encryption-key rotation window (see the runbook).
# TASKDESK_ENCRYPTION_KEY_PREVIOUS=

# Number of trusted reverse-proxy hops, NOT a boolean. The client IP is read
# from X-Forwarded-For at exactly that hop. The Compose overlays set it, because
# it depends on the topology, not on the operator's preference:
#   local / production   1   Traefik directly in front
#   uat (bimats.com)     2   CloudFront -> Traefik -> TaskDesk, measured
# Set it here only if your topology is neither. Measure, do not guess:
# docs/05-operations/proxy-topology-evidence.md
# TASKDESK_TRUST_PROXY=

# Headless installs only. The normal first run needs no variable: on an empty
# database the app serves a one-time setup page, unlocked by a token printed in
# the container log.
# TASKDESK_BOOTSTRAP_ADMIN_EMAIL=you@example.com

# production | development. In development only, HTTP webhook targets are
# permitted. deploy/compose.local.yml sets development; leave this alone.
# NODE_ENV=production

# --- Postgres container ------------------------------------------------------
# Read by the Postgres image, not by the application.

POSTGRES_DB=taskdesk
POSTGRES_USER=taskdesk
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=

# --- Compose-only ------------------------------------------------------------
# Substituted into the YAML at parse time. The application never reads these.

# Substituted into every Traefik router rule. A wrong value produces a 404 from
# Traefik, never an application error.
DOMAIN=localhost

# Which image the taskdesk service pulls. Rollback is editing the digest here
# and bringing the service back up — scripts/deploy.sh rollback <digest> does
# exactly that, and verifies the signature on the way back down.
TASKDESK_IMAGE_TAG=v2.0.0
TASKDESK_IMAGE_DIGEST=

# Opt-in `includeSubDomains; preload` on Strict-Transport-Security. Off unless
# you set it, because both are commitments about your whole apex domain, and
# `preload` is only meaningful once that apex is submitted to the browser
# preload list.
#
# EMPTY OR ABSENT MEANS OFF; `1` MEANS ON. It is not a boolean to Compose, which
# has none: any non-empty value — including `0` — selects the preload
# middleware. scripts/deploy.sh rejects anything that is not empty or `1` rather
# than let `0` quietly turn it on.
TASKDESK_HSTS_PRELOAD=
